Reason:  
• It returns one row per highest‑selling representative within each region, so every rep who ties for the top is listed separately – fully satisfying “include all representatives in case of a tie.”  
• The output already contains every requested column: region, number of orders, total sales amount, top‑rep name, and that rep’s sales amount.  
• Joins and aggregates follow the correct paths (orders → accounts → reps → region), guaranteeing accurate totals.  
• No extra formatting tricks (GROUP_CONCAT / printf) are used, keeping the SQL straightforward and the result set easy to read or further manipulate.